
* res.setHeader('Access-Control-Allow-Headers', 'Content-Type, Authorization, x-company-auth'); // @TODO Remove x-company-auth

* symmetric codec for RPC was nice idea, but doesn't actually work. Code is filled with solutions for browser that would not "load server part". Need to fix the whole architecture.

* If something internal throws VALIDATION_ERROR, it will pass through to the client. Most likely this is actually SERVER_ERROR, so we can't always safely pass VALIDATION_ERROR, only when actually handling input.

* @TODO XXAsyncMethodIssue - find this. sync method "testable" is problematic, need to thing of options or not support sync methods.
* There is an issue that callOn access kind of "finds the service where things live", but we should be able to hint it or soemthing. Linked with  @TODO XXAsyncMethodIssue

* Before test take config snapshot, so that next test runs on "original" config instead. Meaning we don't have to "fix" config after each tests.
  - Search for test 'MESSAGE_AGE_HIGH warning triggers when threshold is set to 0' as an example

* Context is inherited from the test when running inline in testkit. This is not good, should isolate runtime context from testkit, as otherwise inline vs worker mode-s work differently.

* Idea for @mockable to get tests run parallel also within a single describe block, though not sure if it is worth it. But could ID every "action" and @mockable can check the ID and use that to decide which spy/mock to use.

* Logs access test api is not ergonomic, needs helpers
* Logs might use some "checking helpers" more. Needs attention.

* Secret and its usage. Requests etc should not log passwords in any condition.
  This works, but is Secret class even needed at all, we have GGSecret that is used.
  Secret might be useful as GGSchema type, so that data is not string, but Secret and logging that hides it.
  But it can also cause massive issues when storing to DB directly, thought tests would catch it. Needs thought.

* More complex mock/spy expectations - like A,B,C or (A or B) and then C and so on. I should be able to have more power over this. Becomes rather important for cron-s for example.

* Mysql if fails to connect, probably fails silently on startup. Should fail if fails to connect at startup, but behavior currently fine for "config update".

* SDK generation does not work currently.

* SQS - if incoming message validation fails, what to do? Warn? Drop? Currently just leaves it to the queue.

* Warnings for other libraries like we did for sns/sqs?

